Step 2: Start Debugging with AI
Simply ask your AI assistant to debug your code. Try these examples:
"Debug the calculateTotal function—set a breakpoint at line 42, run the tests, and show me the variable values when it pauses."
"There's a bug in UserService. Set a breakpoint, run in debug mode, and show me the stack trace when it stops."
"Set a conditional breakpoint that only triggers when userId equals 'admin' and step through the authentication flow."
What Can Your UI Assistant YO?
Debug Sessions	Start, stop, and manage multiple debug sessions from any run configuration
Breakpoints	Set line breakpoints with conditions, log messages (tracepoints), and custom suspend policies
Step Through Code	Step over, step into, step out, run to line—full execution control
Inspect Variables	View all local variables, arguments, and object fields; modify values at runtime
Evaluate Expressions	Run any expression or code snippet in the current debug context
Stack Navigation	View call stacks, switch frames, inspect variables at any level
22 Powerful MCP Tools
Your AI assistant gains access to a complete debugging toolkit:
Session Management: start_debug_session, stop_debug_session, get_debug_session_status
Breakpoints: set_breakpoint, list_breakpoints, remove_breakpoint
Execution: step_over, step_into, step_out, resume_execution, run_to_line
Inspection: get_variables, evaluate_expression, get_stack_trace
Pro Tips
Use get_debug_session_status first — Returns variables, stack trace, and source context in one call
Conditional breakpoints for loops — Set condition: "i == 100" to stop at a specific iteration
Tracepoints for logging — Use log_message with suspend_policy: "none" to trace without stopping
Multi-project support — Specify project_path when multiple projects are open
Manual Configuration
If you prefer manual setup, add this to your AI client's MCP configuration:
  {
    "mcpServers": {
      "jetbrains-debugger": {
        "url": "http://localhost:63342/debugger-mcp/sse"
      }
    }
  }
  
Replace 63342 with your IDE's built-in server port (Settings → Debugger → Built-in Server Port)
